X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=105779424500899

> but cannot find a device to boot from
[...]
> tsp0 at tsc0
> pci at tsp0 bus 0 not configured

Argh. This will need more work.

What we are trying to fight here, is a stupid bug that prevent multiple
tsp devices to attach (this can be fixed easily - and will be, but this
won't help 3.3-RELEASE installation media).

The trick I gave you prevent the second tsp instance to attach, but
unfortunately also prevented the pcibus tied to the first tsp instance
to get detected.

Could you try the following UKC commands? They will hopefully get you
further in the boot process...

  disable tsp
    (gives you a number, here 132)
  add tsp0
    (give the previous number to "Clone Device", and to "Insert Before
     Device")
  find pci
    (gives you a number, here 48)
  add pci*
    (give the previous number to "Clone Device", and to "Insert Before
     Device")
  change 48 (replace 48 with the number you got if different)
    (then enter "y", "0" and "0")
  quit

And I hope it will bring you further...

Miod

