I'm running 3.3-stable on a PC164LX. It was running 3.2 and running
beautifully. However, shortly after upgrading to 3.3 the machine
(co-located) has been going "off-line". Twice in one day, then not for
another two weeks. I thought that it was freezing, maybe because of the PF
problems discussed earlier (altho I'm not using PF at all).

However, it seemed odd that I never got any error messages in the log that
might be a prelude to catastrophic hardware failure. In fact, this last
time, after waiting several hours to have the co-lo facility reboot it, I
have learned that the machine has actually been working fine all along, but
that the network has been going down.

Obv I suspect the NIC, however this is the only log about it:

